sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task, DECISIONS 4 + R1-R4 (process.stop shape: 209, @swamp/ssh, full intent as inputs). Update shares operation-process-create.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: process:update
  %% kind: process.update
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as Target Node<br/>reached over ssh
  CLI->>GW: process:update 418<br/>--command=… --restart=always
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit process:update 418 --command=/usr/bin/php --command=artisan --command=horizon --restart=always`
  %%> - syntax: `process:update <process> [--runtime=systemd|docker] [--command=ARG ...] [--image=IMAGE] [options]`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - the numeric Process ID and only the fields that change
  %%> Who can call it:
  %%> - the `orbit` CLI and the MCP tool send the same request
  Note over GW: Validate, record the task<br/>keep old spec · #5130
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - your Node has an access grant to the Process's Node
  %%> - a Route that points to this Process keeps the same listener, else `process.route_upstream_changed`
  %%> Result:
  %%> - the new unit or container rendered; secret environment values pushed to the vault key `process-update-operation-5130`
  %%> - the stored definition keeps the old spec until the run succeeds
  %%> - task #5130 recorded with the full intent
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-process-create
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts one Swamp run on serve (Node 209); every step runs there
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - `kind`: process.update
  %%> - the rendered unit, or the container definition without its environment values
  %%> - the desired state, mounts and a retired name when the runtime or name changed
  %%> - vault key names for the environment, never the values
  %%> - the Node's address and SSH host keys; the SSH identity comes from the `swamp` role
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5130
  %%> What you get:
  %%> - the task number, at once
  %%> Next:
  %%> - the CLI follows the task with `operation:show`
  SW->>N: Check the account<br/>@swamp/ssh exec · getent
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - resolves the admitted account home for the rendered unit
  SW->>SW: Prepare the definition<br/>@nckrtl/process-command-assets
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - substitutes the observed account home in public unit content
  opt production, running
    SW->>N: Check the release<br/>@swamp/ssh exec · test -d
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - checks the admitted release directory before activation
  end
  opt systemd, running
    SW->>N: Check required mounts<br/>@swamp/ssh exec · stat
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - checks all admitted mount paths with one argv command
  end
  opt runtime or name changed
    SW->>N: Remove the retired unit<br/>child operation-process-destroy
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - removes the old runtime before publishing its replacement
  end
  opt environment values exist
    SW->>N: Write the environment<br/>@swamp/cfgmgmt/file
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - writes vault content as a root-owned 0600 file; Q-SECRET proved no content in data, diff or logs
  end
  alt systemd
    SW->>N: Write the unit<br/>@swamp/cfgmgmt/file
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - converges the rendered unit file
    SW->>N: Reload systemd<br/>@swamp/ssh exec · daemon-reload
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - reloads systemd after a unit change or pending activation
    opt Vite dev Process
      SW->>N: Publish the dev route<br/>child operation-process-vite
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - prepares the Vite environment and publishes the Route
    end
    SW->>N: Apply the unit state<br/>@swamp/cfgmgmt/systemd
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - converges the running state and boot policy
    opt desired stopped
      SW->>N: Stop the unit<br/>@swamp/ssh exec · systemctl stop
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - also stops a transitioning unit
    end
    opt changed running unit
      SW->>N: Restart if changed<br/>@swamp/cfgmgmt/systemd restart
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - restarts when the definition or activation changed
    end
    SW->>N: Check the unit<br/>@swamp/cfgmgmt/systemd check
    %%> Result:
    %%> - records the running and boot state for the native end check
  else docker
    SW->>N: Pull the image<br/>@swamp/cfgmgmt/docker_image
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - ensures the image exists before changing the container
    SW->>N: Read container spec<br/>@swamp/ssh exec · docker ls
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - reads only the public spec label to skip settled creation on reruns
    opt container exists with a changed spec
      SW->>N: Remove the old container<br/>@swamp/cfgmgmt/docker_container
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - removes the changed container and preserves volumes
    end
    opt the spec is not already installed
      SW->>N: Create the container<br/>@swamp/ssh exec · docker create
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - uses exact argv, working directory, labels and a private env file
    end
    opt a private Docker env file was staged
      SW->>N: Remove staged env file<br/>@swamp/cfgmgmt/file · completed
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - removes the exact env file after creation completes, including failure
    end
    SW->>N: Apply the container state<br/>@swamp/ssh exec · docker
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - starts or stops the container to match the intent
    SW->>N: Check the container<br/>@swamp/ssh exec · docker inspect
    %%> Result:
    %%> - records the container state for the native end check
  end
  opt Vite dev Process, running
    SW->>N: Check the listener<br/>@swamp/ssh exec · ss -H -ltn
    %%> Result:
    %%> - requires a listener before marking the Instance awake; no ownership check
  end
  opt Vite dev Process, running
    SW->>N: Mark it awake<br/>@swamp/cfgmgmt/file
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - creates the awake marker after activation
  end
  SW->>SW: Accept the Process<br/>native assert
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - accepts only the expected runtime and boot state
  alt Process running
    N-->>SW: active (running)
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the Process has its desired state
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event and reads the result step once; Swamp never calls the Gateway
    Note over GW: Store the new spec<br/>Process 418: active
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the stored definition becomes the new spec
    %%> - task #5130 succeeds
  else a step fails
    N--xSW: exit ≠ 0
    %%> When:
    %%> - SSH fails, a refusal, or the state does not match
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    %%> The Gateway reads:
    %%> - which step failed and its error code
    Note over GW: Keep the old spec<br/>task failed · rerun converges
    %%> Result:
    %%> - Process 418 keeps its old definition and is marked failed
    %%> - work done on the Node stays; run the update again to converge
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show #5130
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - asks for the task status every 2 seconds until it has ended
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the current status, and the result once the task has ended
  end
